---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Download — Launcher">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-24 lg:px-10"><p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.24em] text-accent">DEVELOPMENT BUILD</p><h1 class="mt-6 text-5xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-copy">The foundation is ready to inspect.</h1><p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-muted">The current release target is Windows 10/11 x64. Build the native client locally, point the API at a synthetic manifest, and exercise the full verified install path without proprietary content.</p><div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-surface p-6"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4"><div><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-copy">Launcher Platform v0.1</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">Windows x64 · local development artifact</p></div><span class="rounded-full bg-accent-soft px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-accent">SOURCE FIRST</span></div><div class="mt-6 grid gap-3 text-sm text-muted sm:grid-cols-3"><span class="rounded-lg bg-elevated px-3 py-3">.NET 10</span><span class="rounded-lg bg-elevated px-3 py-3">Avalonia 12</span><span class="rounded-lg bg-elevated px-3 py-3">BLAKE3 verified</span></div></div><p class="mt-6 text-sm text-muted">Production installers, signing, and release channels remain intentionally separate from local development credentials and are documented in the repository.</p></section>
</BaseLayout>
